# Database Input Validation

Never pass raw request/query/body values straight into database queries. Validate and sanitize user input first. Prefer parameterized queries / prepared statements over string concatenation to prevent SQL/NoSQL injection.

## Do / Don't

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — trusts raw input; injection risk
db.query(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = '${req.body.email}'`);
collection.find({ $where: req.query.filter });

// ✅ GOOD — validate shape, then parameterize
const email = z.string().email().parse(req.body.email);
db.query("SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = $1", [email]);
```

## Checklist

- Validate types, lengths, formats, and enums at the API boundary (schema validation).
- Use parameterized queries / ORM bind parameters for all dynamic values.
- Never build SQL/filter expressions by concatenating or interpolating untrusted strings.
- Whitelist allowed sort/filter field names; do not accept arbitrary column or operator names from clients.
- Reject unexpected keys early rather than forwarding whole payloads into query builders.
